{"schema_version":1,"objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-SINGULAR-VALUES-LINE-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","pdf_sha256":"4c1a8eb808b32739625aa475c1aad24dc857a3f35fc960504b371487f2850423","account":"fleet02","slot":"B10","run_id":"fleet02-B10-20260925T011508Z-audit-pass3","pass_id":"pass3_exact_constants_adversarial","statement_label":"S2 Linear algebra","tex_line_start":172,"tex_line_end":172,"clause_id":"L172","clause_excerpt":"(a) The coefficient of $z^\\ell$ in $\\det(I+zMM^T)$ is both $e_\\ell(MM^T)$ and the sum of the principal $\\ell\\times\\ell$ minors of $MM^T$, which are the $\\Theta(T)$; by the Cauchy--Binet formula $\\Theta(T)=\\sum_{S'\\subset J,\\ \\abs{S'}=\\ell}\\det(M_{T,S'})^2$. (b) The Gram matrix of the rows in $H\\cup T$ is $\\begin{pmatrix}G_{HH}&G_{HT}\\\\G_{TH}&G_{TT}\\end{pmatrix}$ with $G_{HH}=M_HM_H^T$ invertible. Its determinant is $\\det G_{HH}\\det(G_{TT}-G_{TH}G_{HH}^{-1}G_{HT})$. Since $\\Pi=M_H^TG_{HH}^{-1}M_H$, the Schur complement equals $M_T(I-\\Pi)M_T^T=C_TC_T^T$.","pdf_page":"4","status":"PASS","hypotheses_used":"Finite real matrices; symmetry/invertibility only where stated.","dependencies":"Schur inverse, interlacing, Cauchy-Binet.","derivation_or_objection":"Schur count and Gram identities independently re-derived.","checks_performed":"fresh pass3 direct derivation","downstream_impact":"Feeds product projections/crossing decay.","repair_reference":null,"independence_note":"Fresh pass3."}
